# Build context allowlist.
#
# Without this file the context is the whole project directory — including
# `data/`, which holds the cloned Tools and Data repos and the entity-fishing
# knowledge base. That is tens of gigabytes walked and hashed on every
# `docker compose up -d --build`, to build an image that needs two paths.
#
# Deny everything, then re-admit exactly what the Dockerfile COPYs. `*` matches
# a single path segment, so it excludes top-level entries only; re-admitting a
# directory brings its contents with it. Keep this in step with the Dockerfile:
# adding a COPY without a matching `!` line here fails the build with
# "file not found in build context".
*

!requirements.txt
!src

# Byte-code that travels with a working checkout; `src/` is copied wholesale.
src/**/__pycache__
src/**/*.pyc
